# GitHub Linguist overrides for LukeLang.
#
# Why the language bar shows C++/HTML and not "LukeLang":
#   GitHub only counts languages registered in github-linguist/linguist.
#   .luke / .lk are not registered yet, so ~300 Luke sources are invisible
#   and the bar is dominated by the site (HTML) and the compiler (C++/C).
#
# Until LukeLang is accepted upstream, these overrides keep the bar honest:
# generated site/docs and release blobs should not look like "the project".

# --- Site & generated docs ---
site/** linguist-documentation
site/docs/** linguist-generated
site/dist/** linguist-vendored
site/ops/** linguist-documentation

# --- Release / packaged artifacts ---
*.tar.gz linguist-vendored
*.zip linguist-vendored
*.sha256 linguist-vendored

# --- Archives / vendored ---
examples/v1_archive/** linguist-documentation
vm/stdlib_v1_archive/** linguist-documentation
**/node_modules/** linguist-vendored

# --- Luke sources: detectable once Linguist knows the language ---
*.luke linguist-detectable
*.lk linguist-detectable
